====Noun====
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{lb|en|countable}} A particular discipline or branch of knowledge that is natural, measurable or consisting of systematic principles rather than intuition or technical skill. {{defdate|from 14th c.}}
#* {{RQ:Economist|date=2013-08-03|volume=408|issue=8847
|url=http://www.economist.com/news/finance-and-economics/21582498-america-has-changed-way-it-measures-gdp-boundary-problems|title=Boundary problems
|passage=Economics is a messy discipline: too fluid to be a '''science''', too rigorous to be an art. Perhaps it is fitting that economists’ most-used metric, gross domestic product (GDP), is a tangle too. GDP measures the total value of output in an economic territory. Its apparent simplicity explains why it is scrutinised down to tenths of a percentage point every month.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20180221220246/https://www.economist.com/news/finance-and-economics/21582498-america-has-changed-way-it-measures-gdp-boundary-problems|archivedate=21 February 2018}}
#: {{ux|en|Of course in my opinion Social Studies is more of a '''science''' than an art.}}
# Specifically the [[natural science]]s.
#: {{ux|en|My favorite subjects at school are '''science''', mathematics, and history.}}
