#* {{quote-journal|en|work=Maclean's|date=November 15, 1931|author=w:Winston Churchill|url=https://archive.macleans.ca/article/1931/11/15/fifty-years-hence|title=Fifty Years Hence|passage=What is it that has produced this new prodigious speed of man? '''Science''' is the cause. Her feeble groping fingers lifted here and there, often trampled underfoot, often frozen in isolation, have now become a vast organized, united, class-conscious army marching forward upon all the fronts toward objectives none may measure or define.|accessdate=18 July 2020|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20200718100645/https://archive.macleans.ca/article/1931/11/15/fifty-years-hence|archivedate=18 July 2020}}
